    "word_order": "VSO (predicate-first)",
    "pattern_family": "predicate-first-equational",
    "notes": "[predicate] KA [subject], e.g. PAʻA KA PĀ. Copy THIS pack for other predicate-first languages — then have every construction verified by a speaker; shared order ≠ shared grammar."
  },
  "_review_note": "Predicate-first equational pattern: [predicate] KA [subject], e.g. ʻO ʻOE KA LIMU / PAʻA KA PĀ. Nouns chosen to take 'ka' (none start k/e/a/o) so the ke/ka rule is out of scope for v1. Noun-predicates (he + noun) and PAHU-as-'pushable' phrasing need kumu review before shipping; transform rules are deliberately not used here.",
